# Android Architecture & Jetpack Engineering

This skill defines the architectural guidelines for scalable, testable Android applications built with Google's Modern Android Architecture guidelines.

---

## 1. Unidirectional Data Flow (UDF) & MVI Architecture

Every screen follows strict Unidirectional Data Flow:
```text
           ┌──────────── User Event / Action ───────────┐
           ▼                                            │
      ViewModel ───[ Mutates ]──► UiState (StateFlow) ──┘
           ▲
           └───[ Observes ]──► UI / Composable
```

### A. Strict UiState Encapsulation
* Expose a single, immutable `StateFlow<UiState>` from the ViewModel:
  ```kotlin
  @HiltViewModel
  class FeedViewModel @Inject constructor(
      private val feedRepository: FeedRepository
  ) : ViewModel() {

      private val _uiState = MutableStateFlow<FeedUiState>(FeedUiState.Loading)
      val uiState: StateFlow<FeedUiState> = _uiState.asStateFlow()

      fun handleAction(action: FeedAction) {
          when (action) {
              is FeedAction.Refresh -> loadFeed()
              is FeedAction.ToggleBookmark -> toggleBookmark(action.id)
          }
      }
  }
  ```

### B. Safe Flow Collection in UI
* In Compose, collect flows with `collectAsStateWithLifecycle()` to automatically pause flow emission when the app goes into the background, preventing CPU burn and battery drain:
  ```kotlin
  val uiState by viewModel.uiState.collectAsStateWithLifecycle()
  ```

